---
import painterPoster from "../assets/about-us/painter-three-steps-poster.webp";
import painterVideo from "../assets/about-us/painter-three-steps-v1.mp4";
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import type { ImageMetadata } from "astro";
import dougHeadshot from "../assets/team/doug-headshot-2026.png";
import danHeadshot from "../assets/team/dan-headshot-consistent.jpg";
import marceloHeadshot from "../assets/team/marcelo-headshot-consistent.jpg";
import ajHeadshot from "../assets/team/aj-headshot-consistent.jpg";
import janHeadshot from "../assets/team/jan-headshot-consistent.jpg";
import marcHeadshot from "../assets/team/marc-headshot-consistent.jpg";
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import { pageSeo } from "../seo/registry.mjs";

const teamMembers: { name: string; href: string; image: ImageMetadata }[] = [
	{ name: "Doug Shimp", href: "/team/doug-shimp", image: dougHeadshot },
	{ name: "Dan Rawsthorne", href: "/team/dan-rawsthorne", image: danHeadshot },
	{ name: "Marcelo Lopez Jr.", href: "/team/marcelo-lopez-jr", image: marceloHeadshot },
	{ name: "AJ Biddles", href: "/team/aj-biddles", image: ajHeadshot },
	{ name: "Jan Beaver", href: "/team/jan-beaver", image: janHeadshot },
	{ name: "Marc Applebaum", href: "/team/marc-applebaum", image: marcHeadshot },
];
---

<SiteLayout metadata={pageSeo["/about-us"]}>
	<main id="main" class="about-page">
		<section class="about-opening">
			<div class="shell opening-copy">
				<p class="eyebrow">About 3Back</p>
				<h1>We step back to see clearly. Then we get close enough to act.</h1>
				<p class="intro">3Back is the Team Execution Company.</p>
				<p>For nearly three decades, we have brought an unusually broad range of experience to one persistent concern: how do people make difficult work better?</p>
				<p>We like difficult problems, unfamiliar domains, and work that resists easy explanation. We want to know what is actually happening, what we may be missing, and what the evidence will support.</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="section origin-section section-rule" aria-labelledby="origin-title">
			<div class="shell origin-grid">
				<div class="reading-column">
					<p class="eyebrow">The origin</p>
					<h2 id="origin-title">3Back began with a painting mistake.</h2>
					<p>Douglas Shimp was painting houses. Working from the ladder, close to the surface, he could not see the problem clearly. He climbed down, stepped back, and looked again. From three steps away, what needed to change became visible.</p>
					<p>The lesson was simple: proximity gives you detail, but it can also take away perspective.</p>
					<p>Three steps back was enough.</p>
				</div>
				<figure class="origin-figure">
					<video class="origin-motion" width="1152" height="768" autoplay muted loop playsinline preload="metadata" poster={painterPoster.src} aria-label="A painter covers a small orange defect with white paint, takes three steps back, and studies the result.">
						<source src={painterVideo} type="video/mp4" />
					</video>
					<img class="origin-motion-poster" src={painterPoster.src} width="1152" height="768" alt="A painter covers a small orange defect with white paint, takes three steps back, and studies the result." />
				</figure>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="section traveled-section" aria-labelledby="traveled-title">
			<div class="shell narrow-column">
				<p class="eyebrow">The experience traveled</p>
				<h2 id="traveled-title">The name lasted because the experience was not limited to painting.</h2>
				<p>It appeared in chemistry and spectroscopy, where much of what matters cannot be handled or observed directly. It resonated in mathematics, where an answer must survive examination. It appeared in computing, engineering, games, design, writing, construction, and the trades.</p>
				<p>Not everyone had stood on the ladder. Everyone recognized the move.</p>
				<p>Step back far enough to question what the immediate view is telling you. Then return to the work with a better question:</p>
				<p class="question">What am I missing?</p>
				<p class="question">How would I know?</p>
				<p>Those questions have followed 3Back everywhere.</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="section range-section section-rule" aria-labelledby="range-title">
			<div class="shell wide-reading">
				<p class="eyebrow">Range</p>
				<h2 id="range-title">Experience accumulates through difficult, real work.</h2>
				<p>Our backgrounds include prime number theory, chemistry, spectroscopy, OS/2 kernel development, games and game theory, engineering, writing, design, construction, and the trades. Some of us grew up with computers such as the PDP-11/70 close at hand. We learned by building, testing, repairing, and trying again.</p>
				<p>Our client work has taken us through aerospace, complex medical devices and medical systems, defense and military intelligence systems, manufacturing, technology, and other operating environments where abstract answers do not survive for long.</p>
				<p>That variety is not decoration. It helps us enter unfamiliar work without pretending that unfamiliar work is unknowable. The domain changes. The need to remain in contact with reality does not.</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="grip-section" aria-labelledby="grip-title">
			<div class="shell grip-grid">
				<div>
					<p class="eyebrow eyebrow-light">Operational Grip</p>
					<h2 id="grip-title">This accumulated experience helped bring Operational Grip into focus.</h2>
				</div>
				<div class="grip-copy">
					<p>Operational Grip is 3Back’s operating lens for examining whether people can make intentional, local changes with predictable effect without having to reason about the entire organization.</p>
					<p>Predictable effect does not mean a guaranteed outcome. It means the action is bounded well enough that its consequences can be observed, contained, and corrected.</p>
					<p>The discipline is straightforward:</p>
					<p class="discipline">Bound what you can. Act locally. Observe the effects. Learn.</p>
					<p>Instruction can communicate concepts. Experience cultivates judgment. Grip grows through repeated contact with reality: seeing what happened, testing the explanation, changing something deliberately, and learning from the result.</p>
					<p>That is why we get our hands dirty in the work.</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="section frameworks-section" aria-label="Frameworks and AI">
			<div class="shell editorial-columns">
				<section aria-labelledby="frameworks-title">
					<p class="eyebrow">Frameworks</p>
					<h2 id="frameworks-title">Frameworks are useful until they are not.</h2>
					<p>We have taught and worked extensively with Scrum and Agile. They are part of 3Back’s history, but they do not define the company.</p>
					<p>A framework is useful while it helps people understand and improve the work. When the practice becomes more important than the effect it was meant to produce, it becomes another assumption to examine.</p>
					<p>We preserve what works. We question what no longer does.</p>
				</section>
				<section aria-labelledby="ai-title">
					<p class="eyebrow">AI</p>
					<h2 id="ai-title">Faster tools do not make judgment obsolete.</h2>
					<p>AI gives us faster tools for finding information, retaining context, comparing evidence, and producing work. That does not make judgment or accountability obsolete.</p>
					<p>Faster execution makes the question “How would you know?” more important.</p>
					<p>We use new tools without surrendering ownership of the decision or its consequences. Output is not proof. Activity is not value. Done does not establish that the work produced a worthwhile result.</p>
					<p>The result must answer back through observable effects: in the work, in the customer response, and in the organization’s ability to adapt as demand changes.</p>
				</section>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="section team-section" aria-labelledby="team-title">
			<div class="shell narrow-column">
				<p class="eyebrow">Team execution</p>
				<h2 id="team-title">No head works alone.</h2>
				<p>3Back is a team execution company because difficult work requires the right people to pool their knowledge at the right moment, close enough to the problem to understand it.</p>
				<p>We begin with evidence. We preserve what works, identify the real constraint, and make bounded changes that reveal what to do next.</p>
				<p>We keep returning to the same questions:</p>
				<ul class="question-list">
					<li>What are we actually observing?</li>
					<li>What may have disappeared from view?</li>
					<li>What explanation fits the evidence?</li>
					<li>What evidence would contradict it?</li>
					<li>What bounded action would help us learn?</li>
				</ul>
				<p>That is how 3Back works. It is also why we still enjoy the work: there is always more to learn.</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="team-band" aria-labelledby="team-band-title">
			<div class="shell">
				<p class="eyebrow">The Team</p>
				<h2 id="team-band-title">The Team</h2>
				<div class="team-grid">
					{teamMembers.map(({ name, href, image }) => <a class="team-card" href={href}><Image src={image} alt={`Portrait of ${name}`} widths={[240, 360]} sizes="(max-width: 720px) 45vw, (max-width: 1024px) 28vw, 16vw" /><span>{name}</span></a>)}
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="continuation-section">
			<div class="shell continuation-inner">
				<div>
					<p>Operational Grip explains how 3Back examines execution, bounded action, decision ownership, and observable effects.</p>
					<a class="button" href="/operational-grip">Explore Operational Grip <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
				</div>
				<a class="contact-link" href="/contact">Contact 3Back <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
			</div>
		</section>
	</main>
</SiteLayout>

<style>
	.about-page { overflow: clip; }
	.about-opening { min-height: 660px; display: flex; align-items: center; padding: 124px 0 102px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); }
	.opening-copy { max-width: 900px; }
	.eyebrow { margin-bottom: 14px; color: var(--amber-text); font-size: var(--type-caption); font-weight: var(--font-weight-heavy); letter-spacing: var(--tracking-caption); text-transform: uppercase; }
	.opening-copy h1 { max-width: 860px; margin-bottom: 34px; }
	.opening-copy p, .reading-column p, .narrow-column p, .wide-reading p, .editorial-columns p, .grip-copy p { max-width: 72ch; font-size: 1.125rem; line-height: 1.65; }
	.opening-copy .intro { margin-bottom: 26px; color: var(--charcoal); font-size: 1.4rem; font-weight: var(--font-weight-semibold); }
	.origin-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, .94fr) minmax(0, 1.06fr); align-items: center; gap: clamp(38px, 6vw, 88px); }
	.reading-column { max-width: 620px; }
	.origin-figure { margin: 0; }
	.origin-figure :global(video), .origin-figure :global(img) { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; }
	.origin-motion-poster { display: none !important; }
	.narrow-column { max-width: 760px; }
	.question { margin-bottom: 5px; color: var(--charcoal); font-size: clamp(1.7rem, 3vw, 2.35rem) !important; font-weight: var(--font-weight-bold); line-height: 1.25 !important; }
	.wide-reading { max-width: 1030px; }
	.grip-section { padding: 112px 0; background: var(--charcoal); color: var(--paper); }
	.grip-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: .85fr 1.15fr; gap: clamp(42px, 8vw, 128px); }
	.grip-section h2 { color: var(--paper); }
	.eyebrow-light { color: var(--amber); }
	.grip-copy p { color: #e2e0d8; }
	.grip-copy .discipline { color: var(--amber); font-weight: var(--font-weight-bold); }
	.editorial-columns { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: clamp(38px, 7vw, 110px); }
	.editorial-columns > section + section { padding-left: clamp(38px, 7vw, 110px); border-left: 1px solid var(--rule); }
	.editorial-columns h2 { font-size: clamp(2rem, 3.3vw, 3.2rem); }
	.team-section { padding-bottom: 130px; }
	.team-band { padding: 96px 0 110px; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); }
	.team-band h2 { margin-bottom: 42px; }
	.team-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: clamp(28px, 4vw, 54px) clamp(22px, 3vw, 42px); max-width: 980px; }
	.team-card { display: block; font-size: 1.05rem; font-weight: var(--font-weight-bold); text-decoration: none; }
	.team-card :global(img) { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; aspect-ratio: 1 / 1; object-fit: cover; object-position: center; margin-bottom: 14px; border: 1px solid var(--rule); background: var(--reading); transition: background-color 140ms ease; }
	.team-card:hover :global(img) { background: var(--amber-wash); }
	.question-list { margin: 0 0 28px; padding: 0; list-style: none; font-size: 1.125rem; font-weight: var(--font-weight-semibold); line-height: 1.65; }
	.question-list li { padding: 7px 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); }
	.question-list li:last-child { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); }
	.continuation-section { padding: 72px 0; background: var(--charcoal); color: var(--paper); }
	.continuation-inner { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: 44px; }
	.continuation-inner p { max-width: 58ch; margin-bottom: 24px; font-size: 1.125rem; line-height: 1.6; }
	.contact-link { flex: 0 0 auto; color: var(--paper); font-size: var(--type-nav); font-weight: var(--font-weight-bold); text-underline-offset: 5px; }
	.contact-link:hover { color: var(--amber); }

	@media (max-width: 820px) {
		.about-opening { min-height: 0; padding: 88px 0 78px; }
		.origin-grid, .grip-grid, .editorial-columns { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
		.origin-figure { order: 2; }
		.editorial-columns > section + section { padding-top: 65px; padding-left: 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); border-left: 0; }
		.continuation-inner { align-items: flex-start; flex-direction: column; }
	}
	@media (max-width: 720px) {
		.opening-copy p, .reading-column p, .narrow-column p, .wide-reading p, .editorial-columns p, .grip-copy p, .question-list, .continuation-inner p { font-size: 1.125rem; }
		.grip-section { padding: 82px 0; }
		.team-section { padding-bottom: 82px; }
		.team-band { padding: 72px 0 78px; }
		.team-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 30px 16px; }
	}
	@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
		.origin-motion { display: none; }
		.origin-motion-poster { display: block !important; }
	}
</style>
